  "notes": "The American vocal-group corner of the lane, tracked between the Stockholm Murlyn room and US adult-contemporary sessions: 71–107 for the ballad/mid core and 124–128 for the club-facing singles, all straight with the backbeat on 2&4. Three drum facts are quoted: \"kick on 1/3 plus the '&' of 4\", \"snare 2&4 with a rim ghost\", and \"16th shaker\" — hence the rim lane, the ghost on \"4e\" and a shaker-led perc block. The entry also states \"soft programmed kit with live-feel velocity variation\", which is the only justification for touching `humanize`, so `velocityVar` goes up while the grid stays tight. Harmony is I–V–vi–IV and vi–IV–I–V with a ii–V push into the chorus, and the flat-key major default plus the three named minors give the model four documented tonics, so `keys` is authored here rather than inherited. ⚠ `confidence` is medium because the research rates it high-medium and marks the tempo values **[LOW-CONF]** — they are algorithmic catalogue readings, and `bpm.mode` 88 is this author's centre of the stated ballad/mid band rather than a published figure. ⚠ The **INFERRED** parameters are all drum probabilities and the melody density, which follows only from \"note density low (long sustained chorus notes)\".",
